      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "World_War_II",
      "label": "World War II",
      "description": "The global conflict (1939–1945) in which Nazi Germany was a primary aggressor. The phrase 'we destroy the world' alludes to the global devastation caused by the war, which was initiated and escalated by Nazi aggression.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_549db075"
